:: Widgets Fishing Trash [widget]
<<widget "fishingTrashCatchText">>
	<<set _trash to _args[0]>>
	<<if $daily.fishing.trashCaught is 0>>
		Something tugs on your line, but there's none of the fight of a fish behind it. You reel it in.
	<<elseif $daily.fishing.trashCaught lte 3>>
		Something tugs on your line again, with no fight to it. More junk. You reel it in.
	<<else>>
		Your line gets snagged and you pull up more junk. You're starting to wonder if there's anything down there but trash.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<set _fishingWaterBody to fishingLocationWaterBodyName($bus)>>
	<<switch _trash>>
		<<case "boot">>
			Hanging off the end of your hook is an old boot, dragged up out of the <<= _fishingWaterBody>>, half-rotten and waterlogged.
		<<case "plasticBag">>
			A plastic bag billows up out of the <<= _fishingWaterBody>> on your hook and you work it free.
		<<case "fishingLine">>
			A snarl of old fishing line comes up tangled around your hook. It takes a minute to pick it apart without cutting your fingers on the line <<pass 2>>.
		<<case "netting">>
			A scrap of netting comes up with your line, heavy with weed and wrapped tight around the hook. You pick it free bit by bit. <<pass 2>>
		<<case "seaweed">>
			A heavy clump of seaweed comes up with your hook. It takes a while to pick it all off your line before dropping it back into the <<= _fishingWaterBody>>. <<pass 2>>
		<<case "conchShell">>
			A conch shell dangles from your line, your hook somehow lodged inside. You free it and hold it up to your ear, listening to the sound of the sea for a moment.<<lstress>><<stress -2>>
		<<case "mussel">>
			A clump of mussels comes up fused together around your hook, already dead. You pry them free and drop them back.
		<<case "pondweed">>
			A thick rope of pondweed has wound itself around your line. You spend a minute unwinding it before it finally comes free. <<pass 2>>
		<<default>>
			<<error { message: "fishingTrashCatchText: unknown trash key: " + _trash }>>
	<</switch>>
	<<if setup.fishing.lootTables.fishingTrash[_trash].isLitter>>
		<<if ["fishingBeach", "fishingPier"].includes($bus)>>
			You walk it over to a nearby bin and throw it away.
		<<else>>
			You stow it away. You'll throw out once you're back in town.
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

